# ArtPort Project Rules & Guidelines

## 1. General Project Context
- **App Name:** ArtPort (Art Commission Platform)
- **Target Platform:** Android Only (Priority)
- **Primary Language:** Korean (All UI text, labels, hints, and error messages MUST be written in Korean)

## 2. Tech Stack & State Management
- **Framework:** Flutter
- **State Management:** Riverpod (Use `flutter_riverpod` and `@riverpod` code generation)
- **Rule:** Avoid manual ChangeNotifier or StatefullWidget for business logic. Use `Notifier` or `AsyncNotifier` via `riverpod_generator`.

## 3. Architecture & Directory Structure
We follow a **Feature-First Layered Architecture**. Inside `lib/src/features/`, create separate directories for each domain (e.g., `auth`, `commission`, `chat`, `profile`). 
Each feature folder must be divided into 3 layers:

```text
lib/
└── src/
    ├── features/
    │   └── [feature_name]/
    │       ├── data/         # Data sources, Repositories, DTOs
    │       ├── domain/       # Models, Entities, Value Objects
    │       └── presentation/ # Widgets, Screens, Controllers/Providers
    └── core/                 # Shared widgets, themes, constants, network clients